{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1118781-2e-clan-banes-beast-and-man","id":1118781,"title":"[2E] Clan Banes: Beast and Man.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-20T18:40:17-07:00","id":1118781,"title":"[2E] Clan Banes: Beast and Man.","content":"The clan banes, as per 2E, tend to use humanity. However, Thousand Years of Night (TYN) introduced elder banes. This suggests, to me, that blood potency is a catalyses to banes. Treating humanity as the man, and blood potency as the beast, I think it would be interesting to revisit the banes and reform them. No longer will they be static, but evolve to reflect humanity and potency: a manifestation of the dialectic between beast and man.<br /> <br /> Why? Academic interest. Also, it would mechanically reinforce acetic vampires finding it harder to resist the beast as they grow in strength, and give reason to why, beyond experience, a callous neonate behaves less 'stereotypical' to a callous elder. Also, it nicely ties into the sunlight bane, which embraces both stats.<br /> <br /> How would I do it? Not yet fully fleshed out but I'm thinking the bane should have an effect scale tied to humanity, with effect intensity tied to blood potency. How might that play out? The Nos weakness would no longer be a flat -2 penalty. The penalty would be -(10-Humanity) to interact with X, where X is a table reflecting blood potency. So at 1, only strangers are effected, but by eight, even your touchstone cannot bring themselves to overlook your 'quirks.' Not perfect but a sample of what I'm mulling over.<br /> <br /> Anyway, thoughts, creations, criticism, yet another re-imagining of the Venture Bane, fire away. All feedback welcome. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T19:41:25-07:00","id":1118803,"title":"","content":"So basically expanding and tweaking the sunlight mechanics to cover the clan banes too (and presumably also the banes acquired through Detachment, since that's part of the Mekhet bane)? Sounds like a fair bit of work, but the potential for interesting results definitely has me curious...<br /> <br /> But once again the Ventrue bane in particular seems difficult... it'd have to interact with Touchstones in a <i>significantly</i> more nuanced way if you wanted to keep the spirit of the idea in place. With the Gangrel I could almost imagine tweaking their Bane into turning the roll to resist Frenzy into an Extended Action, with each roll representing a turn and the number of required successes being the factor that scales, but I'm a bit too tired at the moment to give that much focus. Plus, that might be a tad wonky to implement at the table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":3946,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","user":"Sconce","date":". 07-20-2017, 10:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T13:47:53-07:00","id":1119065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sconce</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1118781-2e-clan-banes-beast-and-man?p=1118803#post1118803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So basically expanding and tweaking the sunlight mechanics to cover the clan banes too.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is where last night's rambling led me. :P However, I don't mind taking TYN's route either. Curse One actives at Humanity six, BP 1. It upgrades if you ever get to BP 3 or Humanity 5. And so on and so forth. Less dynamic but maybe more usable at the table.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't be keen on an extended action roll but I can see what you intended. One key point you raise is that we couldn't just amp old banes. This model would need a new set of banes, inspired by the old but operating differently.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}